      "question": "Why doesn't Buttondown capture the full referrer URL when someone subscribes via an embedded form?",
      "answer": "This is a limitation of how browsers handle HTML `<form>` submissions. Unlike elements like `<a>`, `<img>`, and `<iframe>`, the `<form>` element does not support the `referrerpolicy` attribute — it's simply [not part of the HTML spec](https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/4320). Because of this, browsers only send the origin (e.g. `https://example.com`) rather than the full page URL (e.g. `https://example.com/blog/my-post`) when a form is submitted.\n\nIf you need full referrer URL tracking, consider using Buttondown's [iframe embed](#embedding-an-iframe) or the [web component embed](https://buttondown.com/settings/embedding), both of which can capture the full page URL."
